<title>USA: Weyerhaeuser exploring sale of mortgage unit.</title>
<headline>Weyerhaeuser exploring sale of mortgage unit.</headline>
<dateline>FEDERAL WAY, Wash. 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Weyerhaeuser Co said Monday it retained Goldman Sachs &amp; Co to explore the possible sale of its Weyerhaeuser Mortgage Co subsidiary.</p>
<p>Weyerhaeuser did not comment on the timing or potential sale price of the business.</p>
<p>Weyerhaeuser Mortgage, which employs 1,500 workers in 58 offices, focuses on mortgage loan origination and servicing.</p>
<p>For the eight months ended August 31, Weyerhaeuser Mortgage originated $2.1 billion in residential first mortgages.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
